Z||000001||tgowens||05-23-2001||01:23 AM||||the Western Regional show will be in San Leandro July 13-15 - more info on the CFOG web site  <A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> <P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">              </A><P>87 GT - 2.8L Gold automatic<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Blue automatic<BR>87 GT - 3.4L Blue 5-speed Getrag<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Med. Red Met. 5-speed Getrag<BR>88 Coupe - 2.5L Red automatic||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||05-23-2001||10:02 AM||||You might want to check out the Sacramento area club. Also my dad has been trying to get a Central Valley club going. He's in Modesto area.  Email me for phone # if you are interested in contacting him. (He also owns a Big O tire store, he can hook you up on tires and rims)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||05-23-2001||11:32 AM||||Lots of stuff in northern CA.  We just had two events.<P>There was a central CA. Pontiac, Olds, Buick show in Madera a couple of weeks ago.  Three Fieros from Sacramento went, one from Golden Gate (San Francisco) and one local owner.<P>We had 17 Fieros at Sears Point Raceway last Sunday in a "car corral" at the historic races. (Pictures soon, hopefully)<P>Since you're in the Bay Area, I'd suggest joining one of those clubs, or even our Sacramento club, and have some fun.<BR> <BR>Stimpy: That 3.8 SC still around?<P>Ed, President<BR>Northern CA Chpt., FOCOA||||reg||1
